# Meshes are not tracked by default — they are large, numerous and usually
# generated locally. The exception is any mesh a CI case reads: a runner
# clones the repository and nothing else, so a mesh that exists only on a
# developer's machine makes its case fail with "Msh file not found".
# Un-ignore those explicitly, one per case (git cannot descend into an
# excluded directory, hence the directory-by-directory pattern).
meshes/*
!meshes/gmsh_grids/
meshes/gmsh_grids/*
!meshes/gmsh_grids/hexa_TFI_RTB20x20.msh

# Run output of a CI case: regenerated by every run. What gets committed is
# the reference in test/CI-ref/, never the run itself — so that `git add
# test/CI-runs` after adding a case picks up the deck only.
test/CI-runs/**/output/
